---
import Site from '../../layouts/Site.astro';
import PageHeader from '../../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { release, url } from '../../lib/publication';
const states = release.geographies.filter(g => ['state', 'union_territory', 'ut'].includes(g.type)).sort((a,b) => a.name.localeCompare(b.name));
const stateCount = states.filter(g => g.type === 'state').length;
const utCount = states.length - stateCount;
const groups = [...new Set(states.map(g => g.name[0].toUpperCase()))];
---
<Site title="States and union territories"><PageHeader title="Find your place" eyebrow="State & UT directory" description="Start with a place. Each record makes local evidence and its gaps visible; a broad regional rainfall report is never presented as a state reading." />
<section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="atlas-coverage"><div class="atlas-kpi"><p class="eyebrow">Official roster</p><strong>{stateCount}</strong><p>States in the reviewed National Portal name list.</p></div><div class="atlas-kpi"><p class="eyebrow">Official roster</p><strong>{utCount}</strong><p>Union territories in that list.</p></div><div class="atlas-kpi"><p class="eyebrow">Local evidence</p><strong>{states.filter(g => release.observations.some(o => o.geographyId === g.id)).length}</strong><p>Places with approved state or UT measurements in this release.</p></div></div><p class="small muted">Roster names: <a href={url('/sources/E-INDIA-ROSTER-20260923/')}>National Portal evidence record ↗</a>, page last reviewed 23 September 2026. URL slugs are internal IDs. Official LGD codes and boundaries have not been joined.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">Browse alphabetically</p><h2>36 place records</h2></div><p>“Coverage pending” describes this publication’s evidence, not the condition of water in that place.</p></div><nav aria-label="Jump to letter" class="inline-list">{groups.map(letter => <a href={`#letter-${letter}`}>{letter}</a>)}</nav>{groups.map(letter => <section class="directory-group" id={`letter-${letter}`} aria-labelledby={`heading-${letter}`}><h3 id={`heading-${letter}`}>{letter}</h3><div class="coverage-grid">{states.filter(g => g.name.startsWith(letter)).map(g => <a class="coverage-card" href={url(`/states/${g.slug}/`)}><span class="eyebrow">{g.type === 'state' ? 'State' : 'Union territory'}</span><strong>{g.name}</strong><span>{release.observations.some(o => o.geographyId === g.id) ? 'Reviewed measurements available' : 'Local evidence pending'} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></a>)}</div></section>)}</div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="shell grid-2"><article class="editorial-card"><h3>Why the regional chart cannot answer locally</h3><p>IMD homogeneous regions use meteorological boundaries and summarize many places. A state can have very different conditions within it; its own dated observation is required.</p><a href={url('/explore/')}>Explore the approved observations ↗</a></article><article class="editorial-card"><h3>Where district pages begin</h3><p>District names and boundaries change. The next layer needs a versioned administrative code and a source measured over that exact geography.</p><a href={url('/districts/')}>Read the district coverage rule ↗</a></article></div></section></Site>
